menu "Prusa Remote Display display"

    config PRD_DISPLAY_TEST_PATTERNS
        bool "Compile display validation test patterns"
        default n
        help
            Compiles the static display-validation patterns used during
            Milestone 1 Phase C bring-up (corner markers, colour bars,
            checkerboard, gradient, flat colours).

            These are diagnostics, not product UI. Enable only in the
            hardware-validation profile; the debug and release profiles must
            leave this off so no validation code reaches a product image.

            Selected by sdkconfig.defaults.hardware-validation rather than an
            environment variable, so the setting is visible in the generated
            sdkconfig and cannot silently disappear from a build.

    choice PRD_DISPLAY_TUNING_MODE
        prompt "Panel tuning mode"
        default PRD_DISPLAY_TUNING_VENDOR_GAMMA_ONLY
        help
            Which initialisation the display component applies after ESP-IDF's
            generic ST7789 init.

            Gamma-only is the accepted default for this board (Milestone 1
            Phase C1). The remaining modes exist solely to reproduce the A/B
            comparison and are selectable only when the hardware-validation
            test patterns are compiled in, so a debug or release image cannot
            pick a rejected experimental mode.

        config PRD_DISPLAY_TUNING_VENDOR_GAMMA_ONLY
            bool "Gamma-only: PVGAMCTRL (E0h) + NVGAMCTRL (E1h) - ACCEPTED DEFAULT"
            help
                Applies the panel-specific gamma tables and nothing else.
                Phase C1 showed this is the entire benefit of the vendor
                sequence: it improves the accent colour and the black level
                with no side effects.

        config PRD_DISPLAY_TUNING_GENERIC
            bool "A - generic ESP-IDF init only (A/B control)"
            depends on PRD_DISPLAY_TEST_PATTERNS
            help
                Retained only as the Phase C1 control. Leaves the panel on
                power-on defaults: dull accent and an elevated black level.

        config PRD_DISPLAY_TUNING_VENDOR_EXACT
            bool "B - vendor sequence byte-for-byte (REJECTED)"
            depends on PRD_DISPLAY_TEST_PATTERNS
            help
                REJECTED in Phase C1: corrupts the accent colour and flips
                orientation. Reproduces the vendor's 0xD0 length-1 defect
                uncorrected. Kept only so the A/B result can be reproduced.

        config PRD_DISPLAY_TUNING_VENDOR_ANALOGUE_GAMMA
            bool "D - vendor analogue/power/VCOM + gamma (REJECTED)"
            depends on PRD_DISPLAY_TEST_PATTERNS
            help
                REJECTED in Phase C1: same corruption as mode B even with the
                0xD0 parameter length corrected against the datasheet. Kept
                only so the A/B result can be reproduced.

    endchoice

    choice PRD_DISPLAY_VALIDATION_FLOW
        prompt "Display validation flow"
        depends on PRD_DISPLAY_TEST_PATTERNS
        default PRD_DISPLAY_FLOW_PATTERN_CYCLE
        help
            Which bring-up flow the hardware-validation image runs. Modelled as
            a choice rather than independent booleans so exactly one is ever
            active: during Phase C a configuration that silently failed to take
            effect cost real bench time, and overlapping flags are the same
            class of fault.

        config PRD_DISPLAY_FLOW_PATTERN_CYCLE
            bool "Cycle the static test patterns (default)"
            help
                The general-purpose display check from Phase C: every static
                pattern in turn at the validated SPI clock.

        config PRD_DISPLAY_COLOUR_AB
            bool "Hold the static colour comparison chart"
            help
                Draws the Phase C1 comparison chart once and holds it, so the
                panel can be photographed under stable conditions.

        config PRD_DISPLAY_CLOCK_SWEEP
            bool "Sweep SPI clock frequencies"
            help
                A repeating sweep over the candidate SPI clock frequencies,
                re-initialising the panel at each step. Used to establish the
                highest stable clock and, because each step is a full
                init/deinit, to exercise repeated initialisation.

        config PRD_DISPLAY_BRIGHTNESS_TEST
            bool "Cycle the backlight brightness steps and fades"
            help
                Milestone 1 Phase D: holds a static pattern and walks the
                backlight through off, the minimum useful level, 10/25/50/75/100
                %, then a smooth fade up and a smooth fade down. Used to
                validate polarity, true full-off, monotonicity, the usable
                low-brightness floor and fade smoothness.

        config PRD_DISPLAY_BACKLIGHT_FREQ_SWEEP
            bool "Sweep backlight PWM frequencies"
            help
                Milestone 1 Phase D: re-times the LEDC timer through the
                candidate PWM frequencies without touching the panel, holding
                each at a moderate and then a low duty cycle. Used to select the
                production frequency on visible flicker, phone-camera banding
                and audible noise.

    endchoice

endmenu
